{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling the empty input-to-output edge adds a shallow path and gave large gains on all datasets, whereas replacing an existing op often hurt."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the residual skip on edge 3 with a conv removes the identity shortcut and caused large drops (-16/-16/-9 and -11/-6/-11)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where there was none yields the largest gains (up to +53 C10), more than swapping a conv for a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the residual skip in conv-heavy cells is catastrophic (-26 to -34 C100), worse than deleting a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "A second skip to the output is redundant when edge 3 already provides a residual path, so the gain vanishes."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 empty, removing edge 5 cuts all deep paths to the output and collapses accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a useful skip with parameter-free pooling loses both the shortcut and capacity, dropping more than replacing a conv or none."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a harmful avg_pool for a skip gives larger gains than swapping a conv for a skip."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the skip on edge 1 with a conv removes a cheap shortcut to node 2 and mostly hurt, unlike replacing none or avg_pool."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells there is little learned depth for a residual to help optimize, so adding a skip gives only small gains."}], "tok": 18272, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "no